  <section class="hero" id="overview"><div class="eyebrow">EARTH INTELLIGENCE WORKSPACE · VERSION 3.7.2</div><h1>Project guide, setup, diagnostics and API keys</h1><p>EARTHSCOPE combines an interactive globe/map, public Earth-observation feeds, weather and hazard context, location-aware AI, global taxonomy discovery, farm planning calculators, food exploration, road-trip routing, field-boundary drawing, collections, time-aware imagery tools and an experimental 3D driving sandbox. This guide explains the codebase, how to deploy it on cPanel, which credentials you actually need, where to obtain them and what the app can—and cannot—conclude from each dataset.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#keys">Get API keys ↗</a><a class="btn" href="#quickstart">Install guide ↓</a><a class="btn" href="#architecture">Project files ↓</a><a class="btn" href="https://earthscope.yantraiot.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project site ↗</a><a class="btn" href="health.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Server health ↗</a></div><div class="notice"><strong>Credentials are optional for many features.</strong> Do not buy or create keys for services that don't require them. Save real credentials only in the private server-side <code>config.local.php</code>; never paste secrets into JavaScript, screenshots, chat, Git or a public ZIP.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="quickstart"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Quick start</h2><p class="section-intro">For a first deployment, follow the sequence below. Start with public feeds, then add optional integrations one at a time.</p>
    <div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><h3>Upload the project</h3><p>Back up your existing website, upload the ZIP, and extract the contents of <code>EARTHSCOPE_GodView_FullStack/</code> into your subdomain's document root. The live entry point is <code>index.php</code>.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><h3>Check PHP hosting capabilities</h3><p>Use a currently supported PHP 8.x version where available. Enable outbound HTTPS through cURL (recommended) or PHP streams, and enable PDO MySQL if you want persistent saved places. External service requests need an internet connection.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><h3>Configure secrets privately</h3><p>Copy <code>config.local.php.example</code> to <code>config.local.php</code> in the same directory as <code>config.php</code>. Fill in only the credentials you choose to use. The real config file is excluded by <code>.gitignore</code> and denied by the included Apache rules.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><h3>Set up saved-place storage (optional but recommended)</h3><p>Create a MySQL database and user in cPanel, grant the user access to that database, import <code>sql/schema.sql</code> using phpMyAdmin, then fill in <code>db_host</code>, <code>db_name</code>, <code>db_user</code> and <code>db_pass</code>. Without it, public feeds still work but the Saved Places database feature is unavailable.</p></div></div>
    <div class="step"><div class="num">5</div><div><h3>Open and verify</h3><p>Visit the website over HTTPS, reload with Ctrl+F5, open Data Sources and check source status. Test map search, click-to-pin, current weather, crop search and one report print. Add optional API keys only where you need the corresponding feature.</p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="keys"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>API keys: what you need and where to get them</h2><p class="section-intro">No single API key unlocks everything. The current project configuration has optional service keys, including API Ninjas for additional data tools, plus database credentials for saved places. The v3.0 Studio photo-identification tool also needs an OpenRouter vision model ID. Public services below do not need an app-specific key in this version.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card"><span class="pill optional">OPTIONAL · AI</span><h3>OpenRouter API key</h3><p>Enables the Ask Earth assistant and AI-assisted expansion of broad plant queries (for example, “winter fruit”). It also enables server-side text-to-speech if the chosen model and endpoint are currently available. Without the key, direct taxonomy search and browser speech fallback can still work.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://openrouter.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Create/sign in ↗</a><a href="https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manage API keys ↗</a><a href="https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">API docs ↗</a></div><p class="small"><b>Config fields:</b> <code>openrouter_api_key</code>, <code>openrouter_model</code>, optional <code>openrouter_vision_model</code>. Set <code>openrouter_site_url</code> to your real HTTPS website URL. For image identification, set <code>openrouter_vision_model</code> to a vision-capable model ID available to your account. Model IDs, limits, free availability and pricing can change.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="pill optional">OPTIONAL · FIRE HOTSPOTS</span><h3>NASA FIRMS MAP_KEY</h3><p>Required for the project's NASA FIRMS near-real-time satellite fire/hotspot endpoint. It is free to request by email, subject to service limits. The rest of the map and other hazard feeds continue to function if this key is absent.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Request free MAP_KEY ↗</a><a href="https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/content/academy/data_api/firms_api_use.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official API guide ↗</a></div><p class="small"><b>Config field:</b> <code>firms_map_key</code><br>Copy the MAP_KEY delivered to your email; do not share it publicly.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="pill optional">OPTIONAL · INDIA MARKETS</span><h3>data.gov.in API key</h3><p>Enables the India mandi-price integration for the currently configured daily commodity/market price dataset. You need a portal account and a generated API key. If you farm outside India, this does not add local price data for your country; a separate market source would be needed.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://data.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open OGD India portal ↗</a><a href="https://www.data.gov.in/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official help and account guidance ↗</a><a href="https://www.data.gov.in/resource/current-daily-price-various-commodities-various-markets-mandi" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mandi dataset ↗</a></div><p class="small"><b>Config field:</b> <code>data_gov_in_api_key</code><br>After signing in, use the portal's API key/generate-key option. The exact placement of account controls can change.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="pill">OPTIONAL ACCOUNT · NOT AN APP API KEY</span><h3>NASA Earthdata Login</h3><p>The NISAR view searches catalogue metadata without putting an Earthdata key into this app. A free Earthdata Login may be required for downloading certain actual data products from NASA-affiliated archives; it is not a general-purpose API key for the current catalogue search.</p><div class="links"><a href="https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/users/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Create Earthdata account ↗</a><a href="https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/documentation/for_users/how_to_register" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Registration guide ↗</a></div></article>
    </div>
    <div class="notice"><strong>You do not need keys for these current integrations</strong>Open-Meteo forecast/historical weather; GBIF taxonomy/species lookup; Photon/Nominatim geocoding; USGS earthquakes; NASA EONET natural events; NASA CMR catalogue discovery; RainViewer's current past-radar frames; GDELT article search; OpenStreetMap/Overpass nearby places and standard tiles; NASA GIBS imagery. Follow each provider's usage, attribution and fair-use policies. Esri World Imagery is used by the optional 3D driving lab and is not Google imagery.</div>
    <h3 style="margin-top:20px">Where each value goes</h3><p>Open <code>config.local.php.example</code>, copy it to <code>config.local.php</code>, then update fields on the server. Do not edit <code>config.php</code> for private credentials; it supplies safe defaults.</p>
    <pre class="code">'openrouter_api_key' => 'YOUR_OPENROUTER_KEY',
'openrouter_model' => 'YOUR_AVAILABLE_OPENROUTER_MODEL',
'openrouter_vision_model' => 'YOUR_VISION_CAPABLE_MODEL_ID',
'openrouter_site_url' => 'https://your-real-domain.example',
'openrouter_app_name' => 'EARTHSCOPE Earth Intelligence',
'firms_map_key' => 'YOUR_NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY',
'data_gov_in_api_key' => 'YOUR_DATA_GOV_IN_KEY',
'api_ninjas_api_key' => 'YOUR_NEW_API_NINJAS_KEY',
'api_ninjas_mcp_endpoint' => 'https://mcp.api-ninjas.com/mcp',
'nominatim_user_agent' => 'EARTHSCOPE/1.8 (contact: you@example.com)',

// Database values are required only for MySQL-backed Saved Places:
'db_host' => 'localhost',
'db_name' => 'CPANEL_DATABASE_NAME',
'db_user' => 'CPANEL_DATABASE_USER',
'db_pass' => 'DATABASE_PASSWORD',</pre>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Never put these keys in index.php, app.js, a URL shared to users, or the browser console.</strong> These three service keys are read by PHP on the server. Keep <code>config.local.php</code> private and rotate any key that has been exposed.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="config"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Configuration reference</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Required?</th><th>Used for / notes</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>openrouter_api_key</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Ask Earth, broad AI-assisted plant-query expansion and optional server-side TTS.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>openrouter_model</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Model for chat/discovery. Choose an active model available on your OpenRouter account.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>openrouter_vision_model</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Vision-capable model for Studio image-based plant/crop candidate analysis. Must support image input for the selected account/key; the endpoint applies 1.8 MB input size limit and rate limit.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>openrouter_tts_model</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Speech model. Endpoint/model access may change; browser speech is the fallback.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>openrouter_site_url</code> / <code>openrouter_app_name</code></td><td>Recommended with AI</td><td>Application metadata sent to OpenRouter. Use the correct domain.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>firms_map_key</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>NASA FIRMS fire detections. Key is requested from NASA FIRMS.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data_gov_in_api_key</code></td><td>Optional</td><td>Daily India wholesale mandi records where the selected commodity/market is present.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>nominatim_user_agent</code></td><td>Set a real contact</td><td>Descriptive geocoding client identity. No paid API key; cache and respect usage policy.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>db_host</code>, <code>db_name</code>, <code>db_user</code>, <code>db_pass</code></td><td>Optional for other features; required for saved-place persistence</td><td>cPanel MySQL/MariaDB + PDO MySQL. Import <code>sql/schema.sql</code>.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="features"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Feature guide</h2><p class="section-intro">Use the main workspace navigation to switch between the following modules.</p><div class="feature-list">
    <div class="feature"><b>AI Earth Explorer</b>Natural-language prompts for a pinned area; asks can use configured AI and source data.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Globe Explorer</b>Search places or coordinates, click to pin, inspect weather context, overlays and natural events.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Crop Atlas & farm plan</b>Species taxonomy discovery, climate screening, crop economics, nutrient math and printable A4 reports.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Food Studio</b>Uses live API Ninjas recipe records when configured, with live TheMealDB title / single-ingredient search and random-meal fallback. No local preset catalogue is substituted. Provider availability, plan/quota, attribution and recipe accuracy still matter; budget is not a live cost quote.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>EarthScope Studio 3.0</b>Pin-based control center, air-quality model, SoilGrids context, nearby mapped nature/markets/food, GBIF occurrence records, drawn field boundaries, area calculation, three-crop economics comparison, AI trip/meal suggestions and local collections import/export.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Event radar</b>USGS earthquakes and NASA EONET natural events; optional NASA FIRMS hotspots.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Rain radar</b>RainViewer imagery for frames the service currently publishes; not a guaranteed future forecast.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>NISAR archive</b>Public catalogue search metadata. This is not a SAR data-processing pipeline.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Weather & crops</b>Current model conditions, seven-day forecast and broad crop-climate screening.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Time compare</b>Synchronized NASA GIBS imagery views for selected products/dates.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Data sources</b>Provider-status and source provenance view; public-source availability changes.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>Saved places</b>Session-scoped MySQL-backed locations; not a user-account/authentication system.</div>
    <div class="feature"><b>3D Expedition Lab</b>Satellite-first free-roam vehicle/aircraft/boat sandbox with keyboard and mobile touch controls.</div>
  </div><h3>v3.1 integrated Studio workflows</h3><div class="feature-list"><div class="feature"><b>Water planning</b>Reference ETo, crop coefficient, effective rain, area, delivery efficiency and planning days.</div><div class="feature"><b>Fertilizer worksheet</b>Converts user-provided N/P₂O₅/K₂O targets into approximate common urea/DAP/MOP masses.</div><div class="feature"><b>Generic growing calendar</b>Cycle milestones based on an entered crop duration, clearly not a validated regional calendar.</div><div class="feature"><b>Mandi lookup</b>Optional data.gov.in market record request requiring a server-side key.</div><div class="feature"><b>Pest/disease triage</b>AI-supported differential ideas with explicit verification and pesticide safety caveats.</div><div class="feature"><b>Location comparison</b>Compare weather, AQI model output and soil data for two selected coordinates.</div><div class="feature"><b>Public health resources</b>Links to the official WHO Health Emergency Dashboard, WHO Disease Outbreak News and ECDC report feeds. No local disease-risk forecast is fabricated.</div><div class="feature"><b>Route map overlay</b>Rendered public road route on the main map, plus editable budget and optional AI itinerary.</div><div class="feature"><b>Voice AI</b>Browser speech recognition and speech synthesis where supported.</div></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="api-ninjas"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>API Ninjas MCP and embedded Data Lab</h2><p class="section-intro">The API Ninjas page you shared provides one remote Streamable HTTP endpoint for AI agents. Its main endpoint lists the full catalog, while domain suffixes can restrict tool definitions. The current embedded EarthScope integration uses selected REST endpoints via PHP so it can control inputs, keep credentials server-side, cache results and show simple status errors.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="pill">MCP ENDPOINT</span><h3>Remote server address</h3><pre class="code">https://mcp.api-ninjas.com/mcp</pre><p>Optional domain-scoped endpoints include <code>/geo</code>, <code>/vehicles</code>, <code>/health</code>, <code>/fun</code>, <code>/media</code>, <code>/text</code> and <code>/dates</code>. The catalog currently advertises 244 tools; count and availability can change.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="pill">CLIENT EXAMPLE</span><h3>Claude Code</h3><pre class="code">claude mcp add --transport http apininjas https://mcp.api-ninjas.com/mcp --header "X-Api-Key: YOUR_NEW_API_NINJAS_KEY"</pre><p>Use the same header field for supported clients. Never put the key in a URL, public frontend code or a shared project ZIP.</p></article></div><h3 style="margin-top:20px">Embedded tools currently offered</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Provider endpoint</th><th>EARTHSCOPE use</th><th>Limitations</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Current weather</td><td><code>/v1/weather</code></td><td>Weather at selected map pin</td><td>Source coverage/refresh vary</td></tr><tr><td>Forecast</td><td><code>/v1/weatherforecast</code></td><td>5-day forecast in 3-hour intervals</td><td>Plan and account quota apply</td></tr><tr><td>Air quality</td><td><code>/v1/airquality</code></td><td>Overall AQI and pollutant data</td><td>Commercial-use/plan rules apply; not a clinical health assessment</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td><code>/v1/nutrition</code></td><td>Foods/portions from natural-language input</td><td>Nutrition estimate; verify labels/allergies</td></tr><tr><td>Recipe</td><td><code>/v3/recipe</code></td><td>Live structured recipe records returned by provider</td><td>Pantry/ingredient search and requested result limits may be Premium-only; fallback is labelled</td></tr><tr><td>Cars</td><td><code>/v2/cars</code></td><td>Vehicle specification lookup</td><td>Documented as premium-only on provider page at integration time</td></tr><tr><td>Country</td><td><code>/v1/country</code></td><td>Country-level statistics/profile</td><td>Some fields/tier access can vary</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="notice"><strong>Security and quotas</strong>The API key pasted into a conversation should be considered exposed. Revoke/rotate it on the provider account before deployment. The app's server-side integration uses the replacement key from <code>config.local.php</code>; responses never include the key. Each upstream request can consume quota; server-side caching reduces repeat calls but is not a guarantee against monthly limit exhaustion.</div></section>
  <section class="section" id="live-data-layers"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><div class="eyebrow">NEW IN 3.5.0</div><h2>Separate soil, crop / vegetation and AQI map layers</h2><p class="section-intro">Use Globe Explorer → Layers. Each thematic layer can be enabled independently; property/product selectors change what is drawn without changing the base map.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Soil properties · ISRIC SoilGrids WMS</h3><p>Selectable 0–5 cm maps: pH in water, clay, sand, soil organic carbon, nitrogen and cation-exchange capacity. The layer is a global gridded prediction, not a farm laboratory test. The separate SoilGrids REST point query may be temporarily unavailable even while the WMS map is served.</p><p><a href="https://maps.isric.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official SoilGrids map service ↗</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Crop / vegetation · NASA GIBS</h3><p>Choose the global croplands reference (circa 2000) or MODIS Terra NDVI 8-day vegetation greenness imagery. The cropland product is historical and cannot identify a field's current crop; NDVI requests a date aligned to its 8-day composite cadence and is not a crop-type map, yield estimate or disease diagnosis. For crop-suitability modelling, EarthScope links to the official FAO SoilFER CropSuit viewer; its selected VACS crop products use modelled soil/climate/terrain inputs and have crop/region constraints. It opens as a separate external tool rather than being presented as an EarthScope tile overlay.</p><p><a href="https://nasa-gibs.github.io/gibs-api-docs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA GIBS documentation ↗</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Air quality · AQI model grid</h3><p>Open-Meteo/CAMS model output displays available US AQI or European AQI values and pollutant fields on map cells sampled for the current viewport. Cells are visualization units, not native model resolution or monitor-station footprints. Values may vary by region and time; consult official local health alerts.</p><p><a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/air-quality-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Air-quality API documentation ↗</a></p></article><article class="card"><h3>Food Studio · live recipe records</h3><p>Food Studio requests real records from API Ninjas through the server-side proxy when configured. If no API Ninjas key is set, a request fails, the plan does not permit the requested search, or Random dish is selected, EarthScope may use TheMealDB's V1 API (development/education test key by default; configure the provider's supporter key for public production deployments): meal-name search, one-ingredient filter plus visible-ingredient overlap ranking, lookup for full details, and random-meal endpoint. Both providers return real provider records; no hard-coded recipe catalogue is used.</p><p>If both live providers fail or have no matching results, the UI shows an explicit error and does not substitute a pretend recipe. Live/local prices are not supplied by this recipe endpoint; the budget is displayed as a target, not an asserted cost. Time metadata is not consistently provided.</p><p><a href="https://api-ninjas.com/api/recipe" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Recipe API docs ↗</a></p></article></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="data"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Data providers and provenance</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Role in EARTHSCOPE</th><th>Interpretation / policy</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a></td><td>Current model weather, 7-day forecast and historical climate grids</td><td>Model/reanalysis estimates, not a farm's weather station. Respect API terms and fair-use rules.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://www.gbif.org/developer/summary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GBIF</a></td><td>Accepted taxonomy records and scientific/common names</td><td>Names and occurrence records do not prove edibility, medicinal safety, local suitability or profitability.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap / Photon / Nominatim</a></td><td>Place search, reverse names, nearby mapped services and street tiles</td><td>Mapped coverage varies; public geocoders/tiles are not unlimited high-volume backends. Provide attribution and cache.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/geojson.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USGS</a></td><td>Recent earthquake catalogue</td><td>Recorded past events only; this product does not predict earthquakes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA EONET / FIRMS / GIBS</a></td><td>Natural-event catalogues, fire detections and imagery</td><td>Coverage, resolution and update cadence differ by product; detections aren't a complete ground truth.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://data.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">India OGD / AGMARKNET</a></td><td>Reported wholesale prices from available mandi/commodity records</td><td>Not a guaranteed farmer selling price or future price forecast. State, district, commodity, date, variety and unit must be checked.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA FIRMS</a></td><td>Satellite thermal hotspots; optional MAP_KEY</td><td>A hotspot may have many causes and is not always a confirmed wildfire. Confirm with local authorities and imagery.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://server.arcgisonline.com/ArcGIS/rest/services/World_Imagery/MapServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Esri World Imagery</a></td><td>Satellite imagery backdrop in 3D Expedition Lab</td><td>Imagery coverage, provider acknowledgement, licensing, zoom and rate limits apply. This is not Google Maps imagery.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GDELT</a></td><td>Search news/article-index results for topics and areas</td><td>Index mentions can be inaccurate or duplicated and are not independently verified local facts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://www.rainviewer.com/api.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RainViewer</a></td><td>Past radar image frames</td><td>Do not label past frames as a guaranteed precipitation forecast; coverage/resolution vary.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><a href="https://cmr.earthdata.nasa.gov/search/site/docs/search/api.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NASA CMR</a></td><td>Public archive/collection metadata, including NISAR-related catalogue discovery</td><td>Catalog search is not the same as data download or processing; some data access may need Earthdata Login.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div><p style="margin-top:12px">A more detailed provider-by-provider source register is included as <code>SOURCES_AND_LIMITS.md</code>; implementation boundaries are listed in <code>FEATURE_MATRIX_v3.7.2.md</code> in the source archive.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="http500-fix"><div class="section-head"><span class="eyebrow">TROUBLESHOOTING</span><h2>HTTP 500 and service-worker recovery</h2><p>Open <a href="health.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">health.php</a> first. It reports PHP compatibility, config status and storage permissions without displaying secrets.</p></div><div class="grid two"><article class="doc-card"><h3>HTTP 500</h3><ol><li>Confirm the ZIP contents—not its enclosing directory—are in the domain document root so <code>index.php</code>, <code>config.php</code>, <code>api.php</code>, <code>assets/</code> and <code>sw.js</code> sit together.</li><li>Use PHP 8.2+ in cPanel MultiPHP Manager when available.</li><li>Check <code>config.local.php</code> syntax; it must return a PHP array.</li><li>Ensure <code>storage/cache</code> and <code>storage/ratelimit</code> are writable by the PHP account.</li><li>Read cPanel Metrics → Errors or the PHP error log. Do not enable public error display on production.</li></ol></article><article class="doc-card"><h3>Service worker cache recovery</h3><ol><li>This release does not clone or cache live responses during runtime.</li><li>After upload, hard-refresh with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>F5</kbd>.</li><li>If old console errors continue: browser DevTools → Application → Service Workers → Unregister, then Storage → Clear site data, and reload.</li><li>Check the served <code>sw.js</code> contains <code>3-4-0</code> and no <code>Response.clone()</code>.</li></ol></article></div></section>
<section class="section" id="architecture"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Architecture and important files</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>File / directory</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>index.php</code></td><td>Application shell, workspace panels, configuration-status flags and JavaScript bootstrapping.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>docs.php</code></td><td>This in-app documentation page with signup links and deployment instructions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>api.php</code></td><td>Server-side public-data proxy, caching, rate limiting, AI proxy, plant lookups, saved-place endpoints and response guards.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>config.php</code></td><td>Safe defaults merged with the private <code>config.local.php</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>config.local.php.example</code></td><td>Template for private keys and database credentials; copy it to a real local config.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>assets/app.js</code> / <code>app.css</code></td><td>Main interface, navigation, app state, interactions and base styling.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>assets/earthscope-plus.js</code> / <code>earthscope-plus.css</code></td><td>Crop Atlas, Food Studio, additional discovery and recent feature modules/styles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>assets/playlab.js</code></td><td>Separate MapLibre + Three.js driving sandbox; it uses external map tiles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>assets/theme-*.css</code></td><td>Light, dark and night theme styles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>sql/schema.sql</code></td><td>Database schema for persistent saved locations.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>storage/cache/</code> and <code>storage/ratelimit/</code></td><td>Server-side cache and basic file-based rate-limit state; keep inaccessible from public web access.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>SOURCES_AND_LIMITS.md</code>, <code>README_CPANEL.md</code>, <code>DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md</code>, <code>CHANGELOG_*.md</code></td><td>Provider caveats, installation steps, release notes and deployment checks.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div><h3 style="margin-top:18px">Server API actions</h3><p>The main frontend uses <code>api.php?action=…</code>. Current actions include <code>health</code>, <code>earthquakes</code>, <code>events</code>, <code>weather</code>, <code>air-quality</code>, <code>climate-history</code>, <code>radar</code>, <code>geocode</code>, <code>reverse</code>, <code>soil</code>, <code>market-prices</code>, <code>nearby</code>, <code>biodiversity</code>, <code>nisar</code>, <code>fires</code>, <code>plant-discovery</code>, <code>plant-image</code>, <code>assistant</code>, <code>speech</code>, and CSRF/session-aware saved-place actions. Requests are intended for the UI; don't publish service credentials as query parameters.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="deployment"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>cPanel deployment checklist</h2><ol>
    <li>Use a staging subdomain or make a full file/database backup before replacing a live site.</li>
    <li>Extract the project root's files into the correct web directory; make sure <code>index.php</code>, <code>api.php</code> and <code>docs.php</code> are in the same app directory.</li>
    <li>Enable HTTPS, PHP cURL or permitted HTTPS streams, and any needed PDO MySQL extension in cPanel's PHP Selector.</li>
    <li>Copy and fill in <code>config.local.php</code>; keep it private. Do not commit or include the real file in a ZIP shared with anyone.</li>
    <li>Create the database only if you want Saved Places; import <code>sql/schema.sql</code> and use a least-privilege DB user.</li>
    <li>Ensure <code>storage/</code> is writable by PHP but not directly downloadable. Keep the provided <code>.htaccess</code> restrictions intact.</li>
    <li>Run through <code>DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md</code>, then open Data Sources and test each optional integration separately.</li>
  </ol><div class="notice"><strong>When updating</strong>Preserve your real <code>config.local.php</code>, database and uploaded user data. If the hosting platform does not support Apache <code>.htaccess</code>, implement equivalent web-server rules to block private config and storage paths.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="security"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Security and privacy</h2><ul>
    <li>Keep OpenRouter, FIRMS and data.gov.in credentials on the PHP server. Restrict dashboard access to hosting administrators.</li>
    <li>Use HTTPS; cookies use HttpOnly and SameSite settings for session-based saved-place operations; state-changing requests use CSRF validation.</li>
    <li>The current saved places are scoped to a browser session, not a full login account. Do not advertise it as a multi-user authenticated system.</li>
    <li>Public endpoints are cached and rate-limited, but you should still monitor resource usage and provider quotas in production.</li>
    <li>Only pass context needed for the selected AI question. Do not enter passwords, private farmer/customer records or other sensitive personal data into prompts.</li>
    <li>Rotate an exposed API key immediately. Review error logs and hosting backups for accidental secret exposure.</li>
  </ul></section>

  <section class="section" id="troubleshooting"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <h3>AI says not configured / keyword expansion doesn't happen</h3><p>Check that <code>config.local.php</code> returns an array and <code>openrouter_api_key</code> contains the real key without extra spaces. Verify account credit/rate limits and choose a model available to the account in <code>openrouter_model</code>. Check PHP error logs without exposing the secret.</p>
    <h3>Fires layer is empty</h3><p>Set <code>firms_map_key</code>, confirm the key email and wait out any rate limit. Other event feeds do not depend on FIRMS.</p>
    <h3>Mandi price data unavailable</h3><p>Set <code>data_gov_in_api_key</code>. Confirm the commodity/market exists in the referenced resource and that the returned date, unit and modal price make sense. A valid API key cannot make a missing market record exist.</p>
    <h3>Saved Places shows a database error</h3><p>Verify cPanel database name/user prefixes, grants, password and that <code>sql/schema.sql</code> was imported. Enable PDO MySQL and make sure storage directories are writable.</p>
    <h3>Search, map tiles or live feeds do not load</h3><p>Open the browser developer console and Network panel; check outbound HTTPS, CDN reachability, provider policy/limits and certificate errors. Public providers may rate-limit requests. Avoid hammering the public geocoder or map tile server.</p>
    <h3>Assets look unchanged after update</h3><p>Hard refresh with Ctrl+F5, verify the uploaded <code>index.php</code> assets use version 3.7.2, and check that the files from the archive landed in the live web root rather than an extra nested folder.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="limitations"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><h2>Limitations and responsible use</h2><ul>
    <li>Crop and fruit scores are broad screens based on gridded climate and coded profiles, not calibrated yield probabilities. Use local variety knowledge, soil tests, irrigation assessment and agricultural extension advice.</li>
    <li>Farmer cost/profit tools are only as good as the user-entered yield, input costs and price assumptions. Market observations are backward-looking wholesale records, not guaranteed farm-gate prices or dependable political-demand forecasts.</li>
    <li>GBIF taxonomy results do not certify edibility, medicinal effectiveness, food safety or ability to cultivate at a particular plot. Never use taxonomy matches as permission to eat wild mushrooms or self-medicate.</li>
    <li>Hazard layers show published records, not a complete safety guarantee. This site is not an emergency alert service and it does not predict earthquakes, pandemics or disasters. Public-health sections link to official WHO/ECDC resources rather than creating an unsupported local disease-risk heat map.</li>
    <li>SoilGrids-like grid data and historical climate are estimates, not plot-level lab measurements. Satellite fire hotspots are not always confirmed fires.</li>
    <li>Food Studio recipe records are provider-sourced, but provider content may be community-contributed, incomplete or incorrect. Nutrition may be unavailable; locally accurate prices are not implied. Verify allergies, food safety and medicine-food interactions independently.</li>
    <li>3D Expedition Lab is a lightweight free-roam kinematic experience, not GTA-grade vehicle simulation. It does not guarantee road adherence, physical collisions, real traffic, validated routes or zero lag. Satellite tiles and terrain vary by location and network.</li>
    <li>API availability, licensing, provider URLs, model names, free tiers and quotas can change. Re-check upstream provider policies before substantial public or commercial traffic.</li>
  </ul><p>For formal source details, algorithms and model-specific assumptions, consult <code>SOURCES_AND_LIMITS.md</code>, <code>TEST_REPORT_v1.7.0.md</code> and the relevant <code>CHANGELOG_*.md</code> files included in the source archive.</p></section>
  <section class="section" id="v350-updates"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><div class="eyebrow">NEW IN 3.5.0</div><h2>Live images, hazards, flights and browser vision</h2><p>Quick Explore dismissal persists across reloads after search or explicit dismissal. Time Compare synchronizes both NASA GIBS panels around the selected map pin and supports additional products. Real crop/plant photos are searched from Wikimedia Commons with creator/licence/source-page links. A new YOLO26n browser detector can analyse selected images and an explicitly permitted camera stream without uploading the image to EARTHSCOPE PHP. A separate GDACS alert layer covers reported earthquakes, storms, flood events, volcanoes, drought and fires where the feed provides them. Open-Meteo Flood/GloFAS river discharge, ADSB.lol aircraft positions, optional Aviationstack, and location-expanded GDELT/Google News search are available in their respective map panels.</p><p>These sources have limitations: disaster feeds have gaps, news headlines are not verified, aircraft positions depend on receiver coverage, and YOLO26n is a general object detector rather than a universal plant species or disease classifier. Imagery availability varies by NASA GIBS product and date. See <code>FEATURE_MATRIX_v3.6.0.md</code> and <code>SOURCES_AND_LIMITS.md</code>.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="v360-live-explore"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><div class="eyebrow">NEW IN 3.6.0</div><h2>Ask Earth · Live Explore · printable source dossiers</h2><p>Ask Earth now has a separate Live Explore control. On supported HTTPS browsers, the user explicitly starts microphone access, speaks a place name, recipe/food request, or regional hazard question, and can stop listening at any time. Spoken place names are geocoded before map navigation; verify the pin. Place reports bring together current and forecast weather, modelled air quality, gridded soil properties, historical climate, GDACS/NASA EONET event records, USGS recent earthquakes, a news-index search, and modelled river discharge where providers respond. Each section shows source links, missing-data messages, and interpretation limits. The report can be printed or saved as PDF using the browser print dialog.</p><p>Each Ask Earth assistant message receives its own Play/Stop button; sound never starts automatically. Generic assistant responses need a configured server-side OpenRouter key. The default/fallback model route uses the OpenRouter Free Models Router <code>openrouter/free</code>, but free inference can still be rate-limited. Live Explore uses separate public-data endpoints when available and may show a deterministic summary without AI.</p><p>Food Studio uses API Ninjas recipe data or TheMealDB's live recipe endpoints and does not substitute preset recipes when providers fail. Food records, source images, ingredients, instructions, nutrition, prices and availability have different provider coverage; confirm allergens. Flood matching combines reported disaster/event feeds and modelled river-discharge data; it is not an official emergency warning. No matching event does not establish that a region is safe. See <code>FEATURE_MATRIX_v3.6.0.md</code>, <code>CHANGELOG_v3.6.0.md</code> and <code>PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md</code>.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="v372-farm-images-prices"><a class="backtop" href="#top">↑ Top</a><div class="eyebrow">CURRENT RELEASE · 3.7.2</div><h2>Real crop photos, regional crop prices and resilient climate screening</h2><p>Crop Atlas tiles query the Wikimedia Commons MediaWiki API by the species common/scientific name and show the source page, creator and licence details when returned. They do not use emoji art as a crop photograph. If a relevant image cannot be verified, the tile explicitly reports that no suitable photograph was found instead of substituting an unrelated fruit.</p><p>The official market-price board now sits inside Crop Atlas &amp; farm plan and groups returned Government of India OGD/AGMARKNET observations by Fruits, Vegetables, Grains &amp; Millets, Pulses &amp; Legumes, Spices &amp; Roots, Nuts &amp; Oilseeds and Other commodities. Category filters use only actual returned modal-price records; values are in ₹/quintal with a derived ₹/kg conversion, plus available minimum/maximum, market, district, state, variety and arrival date. This source covers Indian markets only and requires <code>data_gov_in_api_key</code> in private server-side <code>config.local.php</code>. A missing response is displayed as unavailable; no price is invented.</p><p>Historical regional climate uses the Open-Meteo archive as primary and attempts the NASA POWER Daily API when Open-Meteo is unavailable or rate-limited. The source and fallback are recorded with the results. If both sources fail, EARTHSCOPE does not generate a climate score. Crop-match scores remain transparent screening indices for a limited source-profiled shortlist, not harvest probabilities or agronomic prescriptions. Broader species discovery uses GBIF; suitability modelling is linked to FAO SoilFER CropSuit / GAEZ, with coverage limits clearly stated.</p><p>Release 3.7.2 aligns all static asset versions and the service-worker cache. After replacing old files on cPanel, if old v3.4 cards remain, unregister the previous service worker in browser DevTools → Application → Service Workers, clear site data, and reload with Ctrl+F5. See <code>FEATURE_MATRIX_v3.7.2.md</code>, <code>TEST_REPORT_v3.7.2.md</code> and <code>CHANGELOG_v3.7.2.md</code>.</p></section>
  <footer class="foot">EARTHSCOPE v3.7.2 · Project guide · Data providers and external services are operated independently. <br>Updated for the cPanel PHP deployment with API Ninjas Data Lab.</footer>
